From ead46d9596fb20c63db33a48709b5192da368aa9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:48:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 17/20] qwen3_5 HIP: the looped forward, its rope and the
 sensenova_loop registration

A forward now runs the plan's executions, not the model's layers: the
window and span passes walk loop_plan's 56 steps and name the physical
layer each one visits, its cache slot its own. Inside the mHC window
the streams hold the residual: a layer branches out of them with its
router, runs its mixer and its MLP on that branch, and merges each
sublayer's output back with the learned mix; the streams collapse to
their mean at the window's end on every visit, as the reference does,
with TF_Q35_MHC_CARRY keeping the carry for an A/B. Outside the window
the fused add-rms tails keep their arithmetic, and the seam between
the two folds and norms exactly once.

The rope kernels grow a YaRN pair: tf_yarn_prefill and tf_qk_yarn_rope
read the static table (its attention factor scaling cos and sin, its
words the frequencies) the CUDA rotate reads. A YaRN checkpoint's
bf16 chat text and --vision rows still take Torch's M-RoPE op, which
reads no table: those loads refuse rather than serve quiet plain rope.

The native server registers sensenova_loop over the MLX affine
formats, text only for now, and declares the reply share 0.5 beside a
filling prompt. A device whose activations are not bf16 refuses an
mHC window, and a drafter cannot tap a looped layer: one ring a layer
would alias its passes.
